      },
      "lineNbr": 482,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-30T19:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the domain\u0027s refcount is still non-zero, i.e. the domain is still in use? Is it ok to just allow the host to prematurely free it?\n\nAnd BTW it seems confusing that the function is named pkvm_free_iommu_domain() while all it does is just _put_ the domain, not necessarily free it, and it doesn\u0027t even tell us if it was actually freed or not.",
      "revId": "e5e35b1f833d316c8b9272c7e36380622f20c5dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2875885_acbdecbe",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 46
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-30T19:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Furthermore... What we are doing here is actually allowing the host to clear and undonate _any_ page? Since in fact we don\u0027t validate the pgd address at all?\n\nSo... it seems that pkvm_free_iommu_domain() should do something similar e.g. to free_pkvm_vm_handle() in arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c, i.e.: it should validate if the domain actually exists, and it should validate if its refcount value is 1?\n\n(But then pkvm_iommu_clear_ce() and pkvm_iommu_clear_pasid_entry() shouldn\u0027t use pkvm_free_iommu_domain(), then should use some other function.)",
      "revId": "e5e35b1f833d316c8b9272c7e36380622f20c5dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
